  "notes": "USAGE:\n{切|き}り{裂|さ}く implies a violent, forceful cutting or tearing motion. It is more dramatic than {切|き}る alone. The figurative use with sounds, light, or silence cutting through something is very common in literary and journalistic writing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {闇|やみ}を{切|き}り{裂|さ}く (to cut through the darkness)\n- {静寂|せいじゃく}を{切|き}り{裂|さ}く (to rip through the silence)\n- {風|かぜ}を{切|き}り{裂|さ}く (to slice through the wind)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\nGodan verb ({五段|ごだん}). Conjugation: {切|き}り{裂|さ}かない, {切|き}り{裂|さ}きます, {切|き}り{裂|さ}いた.",
